// LB.
//
// Load buffering: each thread loads the location the other stores, then stores,
//   and each load sees the other thread's store.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence allows, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     Slow allows. PRAM allows it, and Slow is weaker.
//     Local allows. Slow allows it, and Local is weaker.
//     RYW allows. PRAM allows it, and RYW is weaker.
//     MR allows. PRAM allows it, and MR is weaker.
//     MW allows. PRAM allows it, and MW is weaker.
//   the models' definitions:
//     MRD allows. Neither store depends on its load, so MRD drops the order
//       RC11 keeps. This is the zoo's RC11 -> MRD witness.
//     CC forbids. hb = (po | rf)+ has the same cycle, and CC asks hb to be
//       irreflexive.
//     PC allows. As PRAM, with one write per location.
//     PRAM allows. One write per process; each view places the other process's
//       write before its load.
//     Causal forbids. Each store causally follows the load before it, and each
//       load reads the other thread's store: a causal cycle.
//     POCausal allows. Per object, each location has one write and one read of
//       it.
//     WFR forbids. Each thread's store follows the write its load saw, so
//       arbitration orders the two stores both ways.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: none. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  r0 := x;
  y := 1
} ||| {
  r1 := y;
  x := 1
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [Coherence, MRD, PC, PRAM, Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW,
                          MR, MW]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, RC11, RC11z, RC17,
                           OD-LSO, CC, Causal, WFR]
